:: School - night school built [bg-milk-barn]
<br />
<h1 class="ptitle">
    NIGHT SCHOOL
</h1>
<br />
Word travels fast. By the time the first boards are cut, half the household has drifted over to watch, and a few of them roll up their sleeves and pitch in without being asked.
<br /><br />
Nothing can be fixed in place. The children still need the whole room during the day, so the partitions are built to move: rough timber frames braced at the corners with scrap metal, canvas stretched tight across them and lashed down with rope, each one light enough for two people to carry. Salvaged casters are bolted to the bottoms, and a row of iron brackets goes into the floor so each panel drops into the same slot every evening.
<br /><br />
<center>
    <<image 'places/school/interior.jpg' sfw>>
</center>
<br /><br />
Once the frames are finished, you try them out. The panels roll out from along the back wall and lock into their brackets, and the long classroom becomes a row of small work spaces: a bench for engine parts, a cot for bandaging practice, a table for ledgers and trade goods. Lamp hooks hang from the beams over each section, waiting for the first lesson.
<br /><br />
Then you take it all down again. The panels fold back and stack against the wall, the benches slide in behind them, and in a few minutes the room is open again, just the way the children will find it in the morning. It's a tight fit, and somebody is going to pinch their fingers before the week is out, but it works.
<br /><br />
<strong>The night school is open.</strong> Evening classes run from 6pm to 9pm.
<br />
Guests with the teacher skill can be assigned as instructors, and guests and slaves can be enrolled in evening classes, from their NPC view.
<br /><br />
